  {
    "number": 135,
    "title": "Qualify everyday standalone monitoring with real consumers",
    "body": "Refs #30.\n\nThis adds one confined Linux/WSL qualification command for the revised personal-project scope. It uses the delivered hook and Hub, pinned real Pixoo/Nanoleaf consumers, the actual dashboard and fake Pixoo display transport. It covers one/ten-task monitoring, a short 50-task burst, concurrent integration control, consumer/host outages, restart, retained state and exclusive ownership.\n\nThe final retained run at `d9f5e7e1129f048f8caee046f8f6644e043ec6e2` passes unchanged predeclared targets: 400 warm events, hook p95 58/78 ms, each consumer receipt p95 below one second, 151 MiB peak Hub RSS and all 487 hooks below 3,000 ms. Preparation and measurement both run in supervised private namespaces with verified cleanup. Dashboard evidence records an observed disconnection, a second feed and post-outage revision 473 in 798 ms. Eight development and four full attempts remain retained, including failures and superseded acceptance evidence. See `docs/performance/standalone-2026-09-22/README.md`, `report.json` and `attempts.json`.\n\nQ1 review found two blockers: preparation outside confinement and an unproven dashboard reconnect. Both are corrected with negative preparation/cache tests and positive reconnect observations. CI then caught npm living outside /usr on hosted runners; the launcher now mounts the selected npm distribution explicitly. Concurrent H137/H138/H139 also required guide coverage/timeline reconciliation. No source target, historical receipt or CI gate was weakened.\n\nLocal canonical build/type/contract/lifecycle/state/MCP/Hub/setup/dashboard/workflow checks passed, plus nine Python and four Node qualification tests, 37 pinned Pixoo regressions and 39 Nanoleaf shared-input regressions. Eleven OpenSpec capabilities validate; the new three-requirement/six-scenario change is synchronized and archived. The refreshed guide covers qualification, sequencing and concurrent monitoring issues; generation, five maintenance tests, desktop/mobile/browser/print and output-drift checks passed before this final receipt refresh. Final guide hash/check receipt and fixed-head review results are recorded in the delivery comment.\n\nRenewed independent Standards/Specification review and all six current-head CI jobs are required before guarded squash merge. Merged-main checks precede issue closure. No application UI changes; guide edits use the SDLC exemption. This is source/fake-transport evidence, not installation, client, physical or embedded-host acceptance. Public guide publication remains outside scope and still records source `260707019b7ff83d57e31d91ae1e1582c3734589`.\n",
    "state": "open",
